WEBVTT


00:00:22.964 --> 00:00:25.399
Thousands took to the streets
and thousands killed.


00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:30.294
Many peaceful protesting monks have been
killed, some burnt alive and others drowned.


00:00:30.295 --> 00:00:32.506
Foreign journalists have been
shot and killed.


00:00:32.507 --> 00:00:36.344
Thousands of villages have been destroyed.
Rape and torture are a daily occurrence.


00:00:36.345 --> 00:00:38.746
In Burma there are more landmines,
than anywhere in the world.


00:00:38.747 --> 00:00:42.749
Young men are beaten and forced into
the army. Many as young as 12 years old.


00:00:42.750 --> 00:00:44.854
Beheadings and mutilations
are common.


00:00:44.855 --> 00:00:49.390
The Karen people comprised mostly of poor Christian
farmers have been singled out for extermination.


00:00:49.391 --> 00:00:53.194
The military government wants the abundance
natural resources on the Karen land.


00:00:53.195 --> 00:00:58.399
The bloody military campaign against the Karen
people has been going on for almost 60 years.


00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:02.037
The longest running civil war in the world.


00:02:11.500 --> 00:02:14.500
Hey, send them out!


00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:39.900
Let's go! Hey...


00:02:44.700 --> 00:02:47.400
Shoot them all!


00:03:46.500 --> 00:03:49.400
Here, here, I found one.


00:06:32.900 --> 00:06:35.400
Fuck off, okay?


00:07:07.800 --> 00:07:10.499
Looks like dangerous work.


00:07:11.700 --> 00:07:14.784
I'm Michael Burnett.
Do you have some time to talk?


00:07:14.785 --> 00:07:16.899
It won't take long, I promise.


00:07:16.900 --> 00:07:20.334
I was told it might be possible to
rent your boat. We like to do that.


00:07:20.335 --> 00:07:22.534
Is that possible?
We need to get up river.


00:07:22.535 --> 00:07:25.100
Where're you going?
- Into Burma.


00:07:25.990 --> 00:07:29.600
Burma is a war zone.
Well, that's what people call it.


00:07:29.601 --> 00:07:32.279
But it's more like genocide
than war.


00:07:32.380 --> 00:07:37.200
Anyway, this will be my fifth trip in,
so we are aware of all the risks.


00:07:39.900 --> 00:07:42.099
I don't go that far north.


00:07:42.400 --> 00:07:43.899
Let me explain our situation.


00:07:43.900 --> 00:07:47.899
Our church is part of the Pan-Asia
ministry, located in Colorado.


00:07:47.900 --> 00:07:50.877
We are all volunteers, who
around this time of the year...


00:07:50.878 --> 00:07:53.967
bring in medical supplies,
medical attention,


00:07:53.968 --> 00:07:57.599
prayer books and support
for the Karen tribes people.


00:07:58.400 --> 00:08:00.824
People say you know the river
better than anyone.


00:08:00.825 --> 00:08:03.100
They ain't lying.
So, what I'm asking,


00:08:03.101 --> 00:08:06.770
is that we compensate you
for a few hours of your time,


00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:09.799
that will help change people's lives.


00:08:12.500 --> 00:08:14.299
Are you bringing any weapons?


00:08:14.300 --> 00:08:17.800
Of course not.
You're not changing anything.


00:08:18.600 --> 00:08:20.534
Well...


00:08:21.800 --> 00:08:24.834
It's thinking like that,
that keeps the world the way it is.


00:08:24.835 --> 00:08:26.935
Fuck the world.


00:08:29.000 --> 00:08:30.534
Let's go
Why?


00:08:30.535 --> 00:08:33.290
He's not interested. Let's just go.
- Let me try.


00:08:33.291 --> 00:08:35.495
Look Sarah...
Didn't you say it's the only way up there?


00:08:35.496 --> 00:08:37.450
I know I did.
So what do we have to lose?


00:08:37.451 --> 00:08:40.299
Just let me try Michael.
- Sarah?


00:08:48.500 --> 00:08:50.099
Hello!


00:08:50.800 --> 00:08:55.299
I'm Sarah Miller, hope you don't
mind me, coming back here.


00:08:56.100 --> 00:08:59.420
The man that you were talking to.
- I wasn't talking to anybody.


00:09:01.700 --> 00:09:04.599
Alright, the man that
was talking to you,


00:09:04.600 --> 00:09:08.099
asked if we could hire you
to take us up the river.


00:09:08.100 --> 00:09:09.970
You said no... why?


00:09:09.971 --> 00:09:11.799
Can't help you out.


00:09:13.400 --> 00:09:16.399
Well, if you have good reasons,
would you mind, if I heard them?


00:09:19.100 --> 00:09:20.900
Go home.


00:11:50.600 --> 00:11:52.899
Why did you come back?


00:11:54.000 --> 00:11:56.199
Waiting for you.


00:11:59.590 --> 00:12:01.699
I told you before, I can't help you.


00:12:01.700 --> 00:12:03.799
We need to go, and help these people.


00:12:03.800 --> 00:12:05.534
We're here to make a difference.


00:12:05.535 --> 00:12:07.834
We believe all lives are special.


00:12:07.835 --> 00:12:09.701
Some lives, some not.
Really?


00:12:09.702 --> 00:12:12.134
If everyone thought like you,
nothing would ever change.


00:12:12.135 --> 00:12:13.802
Nothing does change.
- Of course it does!


00:12:13.803 --> 00:12:15.449
Nothing stays the same.


00:12:15.450 --> 00:12:17.120
Live your life, cause
you've got a good one.


00:12:17.121 --> 00:12:18.799
It's what I'm trying to do!


00:12:18.800 --> 00:12:20.634
No, what you're trying to do
is change what is.


00:12:20.635 --> 00:12:22.799
And what is?


00:12:23.800 --> 00:12:26.300
Go home.


00:12:28.200 --> 00:12:30.300
Really.
Go home.


00:12:55.100 --> 00:12:56.699
Maybe...


00:12:56.700 --> 00:12:59.399
Maybe, you've lost your faith in people.


00:13:00.100 --> 00:13:02.410
But you must still be
faithful to something.


00:13:02.611 --> 00:13:05.700
You must still care, about something.


00:13:06.600 --> 00:13:08.899
Maybe we can't change what is,


00:13:10.000 --> 00:13:15.200
But trying to save a life,
isn't wasting your life, is it?


00:13:38.100 --> 00:13:41.234
As bad as these people are,
they will eventually lose.


00:13:41.235 --> 00:13:44.534
They can't keep it up against
a united front. They can't.


00:13:44.800 --> 00:13:47.291
I mean, time alone will tell.
But in the meantime,


00:13:47.292 --> 00:13:49.499
we just have to help
hold it together.


00:13:49.500 --> 00:13:51.434
I mean, just the other day,
I read...


00:13:51.435 --> 00:13:53.499
Excuse me, Sarah?


00:13:53.700 --> 00:13:56.490
Where're you going?
- To talk to him.


00:13:57.200 --> 00:13:58.899
He'll probably want his privacy.


00:13:58.900 --> 00:14:01.234
Michael, you shouldn't ignore him.
He's helping us.


00:14:01.235 --> 00:14:02.651
He's being paid.


00:14:02.652 --> 00:14:04.600
He didn't take anything.


00:14:11.400 --> 00:14:13.599
Thank you again for doing this.


00:14:13.800 --> 00:14:16.199
Really from all of us.


00:14:16.300 --> 00:14:18.499
You know, you never
told us your name.


00:14:19.200 --> 00:14:20.699
John.


00:14:21.400 --> 00:14:24.799
Where are you from?
Mohave, Arizona.


00:14:25.100 --> 00:14:28.334
Why'd you leave?
I got drafted in 'Nam.


00:14:28.335 --> 00:14:30.499
And you just stayed?


00:14:31.300 --> 00:14:33.299
It's complicated.


00:14:33.700 --> 00:14:35.299
You have a family back home?


00:14:36.000 --> 00:14:38.200
Father maybe, I don't know.


00:14:40.100 --> 00:14:43.799
Aren't you curious to see how
things might've changed back home?


00:14:45.500 --> 00:14:47.500
Got to have a reason for that.


00:14:52.000 --> 00:14:53.599
Sarah...


00:14:54.200 --> 00:14:56.634
Because of you, we're going
up the river.


00:14:56.935 --> 00:14:59.134
anytime you want to turn around,


00:14:59.135 --> 00:15:00.799
it's done.


00:15:01.900 --> 00:15:03.700
Ok.


00:15:53.200 --> 00:15:56.299
What is it? Who are they?
Burmese pirates.


00:15:56.300 --> 00:15:59.099
Tell everyone to sit down,
don't make a sound.


00:16:00.200 --> 00:16:02.500
Who are they?
- It's all right. Just keep...


00:16:02.501 --> 00:16:04.100
Don't talk!


00:16:39.700 --> 00:16:42.034
Any more of them?
Maybe.


00:16:42.035 --> 00:16:43.699
What you want to do?


00:16:43.700 --> 00:16:46.234
We should keep going.
We've made a commitment.


00:16:46.235 --> 00:16:48.670
I ain't talking to you.
What'd you want to do?


00:16:48.671 --> 00:16:51.534
We're a group here.
If they want to vote. Vote.


00:16:52.935 --> 00:16:55.999
Sit down!
If it's money they want, we'll give them...


00:16:58.600 --> 00:17:00.900
Nobody talks. Heads down!


00:17:09.400 --> 00:17:12.800
Keep your heads down, and nobody looks
at them in the eye, or they'll kill you.


00:18:57.500 --> 00:18:59.300
No...


00:19:04.901 --> 00:19:06.800
What did you do?


00:19:06.935 --> 00:19:10.434
We came here to help stop the killing.
Who are you to kill?


00:19:10.435 --> 00:19:12.499
Who are you?
Let him go!


00:19:12.500 --> 00:19:16.734
They would've raped her fifty times,
and cut your fucking heads off!


00:19:16.735 --> 00:19:18.101
Who are you?


00:19:18.202 --> 00:19:19.700
Who are any of you?


00:19:21.401 --> 00:19:23.499
We're going back.


00:19:27.200 --> 00:19:30.200
No... no, we shouldn't go back!


00:19:31.700 --> 00:19:33.699
Let go.
- What're you doing?


00:19:33.700 --> 00:19:36.034
We are so close.


00:19:36.035 --> 00:19:38.899
What happened here is horrible.


00:19:38.900 --> 00:19:42.534
But the people in there, are
being killed like this every day.


00:19:42.535 --> 00:19:47.734
Michael, this was your idea.
We made a commitment.


00:19:48.235 --> 00:19:50.799
I know you don't believe,
in what we're doing.


00:19:50.800 --> 00:19:54.434
But it's our live.
Our choice.


00:19:55.600 --> 00:19:58.800
You're not going to change anything.


00:20:00.100 --> 00:20:01.699
Please.


00:20:02.100 --> 00:20:03.799
Please John.


00:20:03.900 --> 00:20:06.000
Please.


00:20:17.800 --> 00:20:20.500
Go sit down.


00:21:15.200 --> 00:21:17.214
We'll be taking the overland route
on the way back,


00:21:17.215 --> 00:21:20.000
so there's no need to wait around.


00:21:20.700 --> 00:21:22.699
I have to report this.


00:21:22.700 --> 00:21:24.134
I know you think what
you did was right,


00:21:24.135 --> 00:21:27.400
but taking a life is never right.


00:21:42.900 --> 00:21:45.299
I don't know what to say.


00:21:45.300 --> 00:21:50.100
Maybe you shouldn't say anything,
should you? Good Luck.


00:23:48.800 --> 00:23:50.500
Hey...


00:24:42.800 --> 00:24:46.900
Open...


00:25:03.300 --> 00:25:06.400
So Christ may dwell
your hearts with faith.


00:25:18.400 --> 00:25:21.800
Let me see if I can fix
this little problem, ok?


00:25:35.000 --> 00:25:39.100
Hey you, can you hand me
one of those bandages?


00:25:43.400 --> 00:25:44.800
Okay.


00:26:01.099 --> 00:26:04.499
Get out of here!
What about them? Go on, take them!


00:29:29.000 --> 00:29:31.636
...calling Raven.
Come on, Raven.


00:29:33.000 --> 00:29:34.199
What am I?


00:29:34.200 --> 00:29:37.399
You made me this way.
You're a full blooded combat soldier.


00:29:37.400 --> 00:29:38.999
You don't just turn it off!


00:29:39.000 --> 00:29:41.499
Talk to me Johnny!
You just don't turn it off!


00:29:41.500 --> 00:29:45.500
It's over!
Nothing is over!


00:29:45.700 --> 00:29:49.000
When are you going to come full circle?
I know the reason you're here, John.


00:29:51.000 --> 00:29:54.500
Aren't you curious to see how things
might have changed back home?


00:29:55.200 --> 00:29:57.399
You've done enough damage!


00:29:57.700 --> 00:29:59.699
You will always going to be
tearing away at yourself,


00:29:59.700 --> 00:30:01.899
until you come to terms
with what you are.


00:30:01.900 --> 00:30:03.700
Until you come full circle.


00:30:03.701 --> 00:30:06.499
So, you're just going to stay here forever?
- John!


00:30:08.200 --> 00:30:10.499
John Rambo!


00:30:10.500 --> 00:30:12.399
John.


00:30:12.600 --> 00:30:16.500
John Rambo.


00:30:25.900 --> 00:30:28.699
My name is Arthur Marsh.


00:30:28.700 --> 00:30:32.099
Pastor of the Christ Church of Colorado.


00:30:32.100 --> 00:30:34.099
I need to talk with you.


00:30:34.100 --> 00:30:37.699
It's very important, I wouldn't come
here like this, if it wasn't.


00:30:40.710 --> 00:30:44.199
The morning of the day the group left,


00:30:44.200 --> 00:30:45.699
Michael Burnet notified me,


00:30:45.700 --> 00:30:49.999
that they were travelling
from this location.


00:30:51.300 --> 00:30:54.165
What happened?
No one knows exactly.


00:30:54.500 --> 00:30:57.799
They were supposed to return 10 days
ago, but they never came back.


00:30:57.800 --> 00:31:00.799
I requested help from the embassy,
but they can't help.


00:31:00.800 --> 00:31:03.583
Not in Burma and not in time.


00:31:04.084 --> 00:31:05.399
How do you know they're alive?


00:31:05.400 --> 00:31:08.434
Because we've been in contact
with the Karen freedom fighters,


00:31:08.435 --> 00:31:11.599
who say, they think they know
where they were taken.


00:31:12.400 --> 00:31:15.950
And I was given the name of an ex-military
American local from the embassy,


00:31:15.951 --> 00:31:20.834
who put me in touch with men who say
they've experience in this part of the world.


00:31:20.835 --> 00:31:22.699
Mercenaries?


00:31:22.700 --> 00:31:24.499
Yes


00:31:24.700 --> 00:31:26.799
I don't have any other choice.


00:31:27.100 --> 00:31:31.379
You know the exact spot.
We need you to take these men,


00:31:31.980 --> 00:31:33.899
to where you let our people off.


00:31:33.900 --> 00:31:35.934
When're they ready to leave?


00:31:36.535 --> 00:31:38.400
When you are.


00:31:54.900 --> 00:31:57.399
You know what you are.


00:31:58.100 --> 00:32:01.100
What you're made of.


00:32:02.700 --> 00:32:05.099
War is in your blood.


00:32:06.000 --> 00:32:08.099
Don't fight it.


00:32:09.600 --> 00:32:12.599
You didn't kill for your country.


00:32:13.300 --> 00:32:16.599
You killed for yourself.


00:32:18.400 --> 00:32:21.600
God is never going to
make that go away.


00:32:26.200 --> 00:32:29.000
But when you're pushed.


00:32:31.700 --> 00:32:35.100
Killing is as easy as breathing.


00:33:01.350 --> 00:33:04.626
Look at this fucking place.
Only a fucking ape would live here.


00:33:04.627 --> 00:33:06.934
What the fuck am I doing here?


00:33:06.935 --> 00:33:09.799
Hey, knock that shit off!


00:33:09.800 --> 00:33:11.499
En-Joo don't like the arts?


00:33:11.500 --> 00:33:14.299
En-Joo don't like shit.
I like your sister, Diaz.


00:33:14.300 --> 00:33:16.299
She's got a thing for retards.


00:33:16.300 --> 00:33:18.399
Hey boatman!


00:33:18.400 --> 00:33:21.799
How much longer in this
ancient piece of shit?


00:33:25.400 --> 00:33:27.599
So, what did the Reverend say to you?


00:33:27.600 --> 00:33:29.599
Some shit, about how
his flock gone missing.


00:33:29.600 --> 00:33:30.684
I said to him. Look mate,


00:33:30.685 --> 00:33:33.884
that's what you get when you go
trespassing into fucking Burma.


00:33:33.885 --> 00:33:36.899
That's what you get, when you go
sniffing around other people's garbage.


00:33:36.900 --> 00:33:39.234
You know those generals in there,
making millions, cranking out more than


00:33:39.235 --> 00:33:41.899
any other place on this fucking planet.
- Bullshit!


00:33:41.900 --> 00:33:44.634
Millions, Moron.
How'd you think they pay for that shit all?


00:33:44.635 --> 00:33:47.551
Try reading the paper, Redneck,
instead of sleeping under it.


00:33:47.552 --> 00:33:50.034
Fucking generals, the biggest
junkies of all of them.


00:33:50.035 --> 00:33:51.799
It's noble, Lewis.


00:33:51.800 --> 00:33:55.834
You are?
Those people going in there with no weapons.


00:33:55.835 --> 00:33:58.099
Just books and meds.


00:33:58.100 --> 00:34:00.434
It's noble.
Oh, Schoolboy!


00:34:00.500 --> 00:34:02.434
You stick your noble nose
in other people's business,


00:34:02.435 --> 00:34:04.599
you get fucked up
or you get dead.


00:34:04.600 --> 00:34:06.984
The only reason I'm doing this,
is for an ex-wife and 3 kids.


00:34:06.985 --> 00:34:10.534
And after this shit is over, you can
shove that soldiering right up your ass.


00:34:10.535 --> 00:34:12.099
Try the decaf, mate!
Fuck off!


00:34:12.100 --> 00:34:16.389
And you!... I don't want to die of old age,
before I get there... so move.


00:34:21.400 --> 00:34:24.800
You said something?


00:36:20.300 --> 00:36:21.899
Is it me?


00:36:22.300 --> 00:36:26.199
Or does the air that's coming in,
smell like a goddamn wet dog?


00:36:27.600 --> 00:36:30.799
Fuck sake, I can swim faster than this.


00:36:30.800 --> 00:36:33.499
Am I right?
Real dead.


00:36:33.500 --> 00:36:38.100
Chop, chop. The quicker we get
there, the quicker we get back.


00:36:42.700 --> 00:36:45.199
Those god squatters.


00:36:46.100 --> 00:36:47.899
They come over here.


00:36:47.900 --> 00:36:51.399
Spouting all that shit.


00:36:51.400 --> 00:36:55.399
Expect the whole world to work like
their fucking neighbours. Well it doesn't.


00:36:56.400 --> 00:36:59.599
So, they send in the devil.


00:36:59.700 --> 00:37:02.999
To do god's work.
It's ironic, isn't it?


00:37:04.800 --> 00:37:07.899
Am I boring you, mate?


00:37:08.100 --> 00:37:12.396
What is it? Is it the trip?
Has it got you nervous?


00:37:12.497 --> 00:37:15.598
Cause really, you should appreciate
the action. You know what I mean?


00:37:15.599 --> 00:37:19.099
Got to be better than looking
at the ass-end of a snake.


00:37:21.000 --> 00:37:22.999
Oh dear.


00:37:23.000 --> 00:37:26.299
You really are an uptight bastard,
aren't you?


00:37:27.800 --> 00:37:30.384
You can drop the thousand yard stare.


00:37:30.385 --> 00:37:32.699
I've seen it all before.


00:37:32.700 --> 00:37:36.300
I'm not impressed.


00:37:45.900 --> 00:37:48.384
He's old school, SAS.


00:37:48.485 --> 00:37:51.485
The first rate soldiers,
to be told to go maniacs.


00:37:52.600 --> 00:37:55.699
They call me Schoolboy.


00:37:55.800 --> 00:37:59.099
The name stuck with me,
since sniper school.


00:37:59.100 --> 00:38:02.700
My mates won’t stop calling me,
no matter how many people I shoot.


00:38:29.300 --> 00:38:32.000
What do you want from us?


00:39:17.500 --> 00:39:19.634
One man and a kid, you've
got to be fucking joking.


00:39:19.635 --> 00:39:22.499
This’d all the rebels they put up?
I'm not liking it.


00:39:22.500 --> 00:39:25.634
You're in a fucking jungle, pussnut.
There's nothing to like.


00:39:25.635 --> 00:39:27.199
How you're doing?


00:39:27.200 --> 00:39:29.699
My name is Bieth, this is Tha.


00:39:29.700 --> 00:39:30.934
This is it?


00:39:30.935 --> 00:39:33.099
Yes.
What's up with the kid, man?


00:39:33.100 --> 00:39:36.800
He's good tracker.
We don't need a tracker, we need a guide.


00:39:37.335 --> 00:39:39.134
You know the exact location, right?


00:39:39.135 --> 00:39:40.699
10 km west.


00:39:40.700 --> 00:39:43.484
To north, 6 kilo walk.
- How many soldiers?


00:39:43.485 --> 00:39:45.399
100 maybe.
100?


00:39:45.400 --> 00:39:48.599
What did he say?
- More new soldiers, come tomorrow.


00:39:48.600 --> 00:39:51.599
I know I'm just a white trash
grunt, but I can count.


00:39:51.600 --> 00:39:53.399
Fuck fucking with that 100 strong.
- Alright, alright, alright!


00:39:53.400 --> 00:39:55.099
Let's get this straight.


00:39:55.100 --> 00:39:58.699
We don't engage anybody.
If we can extract these people, good.


00:39:58.700 --> 00:40:01.434
But it's in, out, clean,
or we fuck off.


00:40:01.435 --> 00:40:04.899
